     "page": 2,
     "text": "FAX 14  -- ROI --\nchocardiographic findings continue to benign.\n\n- **2023-01-19:** During an annual physical on January 19, 2023, Donna's blood pressure was I33/87, and she weighed 161 pounds. Routine laboratory tests were within normal limits. Her atrial fibrillation was stable, and she continues to follow a healthy lifestyle with no new cardiac events.\n\n- **2022-09-26:** On September 26, 2022, Donna was seen for atrial fibrillation/flutter. Her blood pressure was 136/84, and she weighed 149 pounds. The echocardiogram was normal, and her atrial fibrillation remained controlled. She reported no new symptoms and her overall health status was stable.\n\n---\n\n**Assessment/Plan:**\n\n- **Atrial Fibrillation/Flutter (normal echo; CHA2DS2-VASc 4; 11 years ago):** Controlled; medications: None \n Donna's atrial fibrillation/flutter, diagnosed 11 years ago, is well-controlled with no current symptoms. Her echocardiographic findings have consistently shown no structural heart disease. The CHA2DS2-VASc score is 4, indicating a moderate risk of stroke. Despite this, her atrial fibrillation has remained stable without requiring pharmacologic intervention. Regular follow-ups are recommended to monitor for any changes in her cardiac status.\n\n- **Social History:** Alcohol intake is approximately 8 drinks per week, which is within moderate limits. There is no documented history of smoking or illicit drug use.\n\n- **Family History:** Notably, Donna's father had colon cancer, which he developed at age 56 and passed away at age 52. This history underscores the importance of regular cancer screenings and preventive care.\n\n---\n\nThis summary provides a comprehensive overview of Donna Kerr's current cardiac health status, her controlled atrial fibrillation, and her stable condition over multiple follow-up visits. Regular monitoring and adherence to lifestyle modifications are crucial to maintaining her cardiovascular health.\n"
